  "id": "OSEC-2026-22",
  "modified": "2026-10-23T21:30:00Z",
  "published": "2026-10-23T21:30:00Z",
  "summary": "Integer overflow in Unix.map_file",
  "details": "ANT-2026-6W9NPC2Q mmap dimension product integer overflow\n\n\n## Fix\n\nUse `caml_umul_overflow` instead of `*` when multiplying bigarray dimensions, which detects integer overflows and raise `Failure`.\nNegative positions are also rejected by raising `Invalid_argument`.\n\n## Am I affected?\n\nIf either the dimensions or the file size in a call to `Unix.map_file` from your code is user controllable then you are potentially affected.\n\n## Score notes\n\nThe vulnerability is in a library, and the CVSS score is calculated [under worst case assumptions](https://www.first.org/cvss/v4.0/user-guide#Assessing-Vulnerabilities-in-Software-Libraries-and-Similar). For an actual application the score will depend on how much an attacker can control the input to this function (if at all).\n\n\n## Timeline\n\n- 2026-08-24: vulnerability was found\n- 2026-08-27: forwarded report to security@ocaml.org\n- 2026-09-29: fix merged to trunk",
